                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A pretty decent game especially if you can find somebody to couch VS with. It does have an online mode but I have not tried it tbh and it should most likely be very empty. I would still recommend Nidhogg 1&2 over this they are a much deeper and more satisfying experience. \n\nThis game works fine and is kind of fun but it feels really barebones. There are some challenges but they really don't do anything special. Get Nidhogg 2 instead if you haven't played that yet and are interested in this style of gameplay. Having a second player handy is what matters most in these types of games.\n\nTwo of the achievements also seem to be bugged and won't unlock as well no matter what I try.",
